            "text": "Scilla monophyllos, the single-leaved squill, is a species of flowering plant in the family Asparagaceae. It is native to Morocco, Portugal, and western Spain. As its scientific and common names suggest, it typically has only one leaf.\n{{Gallery\n|Scilla monophyllos kz09.jpg|Emerging leaf tip\n|Scilla monophyllos kz10.jpg|An individual\n|Scila monophyllos 1.JPG|Clump\n|Scilla monophyllos kz07.jpg|Fruit\n}}"
